<text x="-23.876" y="-94.488" size="1.27" layer="21" rot="R90" align="top-center">Arduino 
Power Line</text>
<text x="-23.876" y="-105.156" size="1.27" layer="21" rot="R90" align="top-center">Pump
Power Line</text>
<text x="-10.922" y="-97.282" size="1.778" layer="21" rot="R90" align="top-center">+</text>
<text x="-10.922" y="-108.204" size="1.778" layer="21" rot="R90" align="top-center">+</text>
<text x="-10.922" y="-103.124" size="1.778" layer="21" rot="R90" align="top-center">-</text>
<text x="-10.922" y="-91.948" size="1.778" layer="21" rot="R90" align="top-center">-</text>
<text x="-100.33" y="-76.708" size="1.4224" layer="21" align="top-center">connects to:
Arduinos 1-8 + BNC 1/2</text>
<text x="-99.822" y="-136.144" size="1.4224" layer="21" align="top-center">connects to:
Arduinos 9-16 + BNC 3/4</text>
<text x="-50.8" y="-143.764" size="1.016" layer="21" align="center-left">The purpose of the PORTMASTER is
to provide an interface between up to 
16 Lickports (Lick-O-Tron), 4 extra
BNC I/O and the two master Arduino 
Megas.
This board delivers power to the peripheral
Arduinos and pumps and provides logical
connections between the peripheral
Arduinos and the Megas</text>
<text x="-48.26" y="-93.726" size="1.4224" layer="21">by Bela Erlinghagen</text>
</plain>
<libraries>
<library name="MasterModuleLibrary" urn="urn:adsk.wipprod:fs.file:vf.kdmJV2YEQuycxh8agCBwng">
<packages>
<package name="ARDUINO_MEGA_NO_SILK" urn="urn:adsk.eagle:footprint:41384819/1" library_version="5">
<description>&lt;h3&gt; Arduino MEGA R3 footprint&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specifications:
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Pin count:82&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Area:4x2.15 in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example device(s):
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Arduino Mega R3&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
